          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5de6d83fd1fc853f5dbc34285200f2cc23e1910e491a19b12f80f78846b0a032:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_52ba082be3a643a49997ee819ae86f10",
      "statement": "util::tool_version never checks the child's exit status, so get_version() returning Err means only that the executable could not be spawned (an availability test, not a version report) and is wrapped as \"Failed to spawn <name>\"; it degrades to the literal string \"unknown\" when the regex does not match. ctrtool::get_version() is the only remaining caller: it probes ctrtool with no arguments on stderr line 0 with regex \\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/ctrtool.rs#L22-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc91465f1f4bc29f7257de16c236c3434b4de927fc9c2d631aa222ffe93bd164:"
