        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_09d33a5d43f0413f9bb92032a92eb73d",
      "statement": "The ctrtool calls report progress with start_action/stop_action (spinner plus a message such as \"Parsing cia\" / \"Extracting files\") because a child process exposes no measurable byte count, while the in-process format crates feed their &mut dyn FnMut(u64) progress callbacks into progress::run_blocking, which switches the bar to a real byte-progress style — so CHD, CSO/ZSO, NSZ and patch work report throughput where the subprocess paths cannot.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/ctrtool.rs#L101-L106",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:849f97c32534baf47415bee878b801b687fe962f299c7e7d53605acf6d1c55d1:"
