      "id": "claim_ce9150f5cd114fca8429cff860c7f27f",
      "statement": "Neither distribution container installs an external format tool: the Arch Linux image installs only base-devel, curl and rustup (removing the toolchain layers afterwards) and the Alpine image only build-base, curl, gcompat, musl-dev and rustup. CHD support works in both because it is compiled in via chd-rs, while CIA support is absent in both by construction since ctrtool is never installed.",
